        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this entertaining party game, the goal is to guess images. The pictures are hidden by tiles that are uncovered at random. The challenge is to recognize the images with as few revealed tiles as possible. What exactly has to be guessed – places, movies, or car brands – is completely up to you. All you need is a folder with images whose file names contain the solution. The game is best enjoyed together with friends or family on a big screen!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can also collect status effects hidden in certain tiles. These either give the finder an advantage for their next image or hinder their opponents. For example, the “Finger of God” effect allows you to use the arrow keys on the next image to decide which tiles to reveal, while the “Chaos” effect scrambles the image into segments that are randomly shuffled and rotated.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game master is responsible for the controls. They reveal tiles one by one or – once a player has given their answer – uncover the entire image and record whether the answer was correct. The winner is the player or team who has guessed the most images correctly while revealing the fewest tiles.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The required folders can either be created by yourself or downloaded from the Steam Workshop, where users share their content. The game itself does not include any images.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Have fun guessing and strategizing together!</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this entertaining party game, the goal is to guess images. The pictures are hidden by tiles that are uncovered at random. The challenge is to recognize the images with as few revealed tiles as possible. What exactly has to be guessed – places, movies, or car brands – is completely up to you. All you need is a folder with images whose file names contain the solution. The game is best enjoyed together with friends or family on a big screen!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can also collect status effects hidden in certain tiles. These either give the finder an advantage for their next image or hinder their opponents. For example, the “Finger of God” effect allows you to use the arrow keys on the next image to decide which tiles to reveal, while the “Chaos” effect scrambles the image into segments that are randomly shuffled and rotated.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game master is responsible for the controls. They reveal tiles one by one or – once a player has given their answer – uncover the entire image and record whether the answer was correct. The winner is the player or team who has guessed the most images correctly while revealing the fewest tiles.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The required folders can either be created by yourself or downloaded from the Steam Workshop, where users share their content. The game itself does not include any images.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Have fun guessing and strategizing together!</p>",
        "short_description": "A fun party game where players try to guess images – with as few tiles revealed as possible. Perfect for groups, featuring hidden effects as playful twists. Who can combine clues cleverly and trust their instincts?",
